            <p>As the Month of the Military Child came to a close, the Iowa Army National Guard Child &amp; Youth Program brought families together for an evening that went far beyond a traditional event. The Military Family Ball created space for connection, understanding, and shared experience, something military families often do not get enough of.</p>
            <p>From the moment families arrived, the atmosphere carried a sense of ease and belonging. Conversations flowed naturally, youth connected quickly, and parents found themselves among others who understand the unique rhythm of military life. For many families, that connection is what matters most.</p>
